Package: dacc
Title: Detection and Attribution Analysis of Climate Change
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-11-01
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Haoran", family = "Li", role = "aut"),
    person(given = "Yan", family = "Li",
           email = "yan.4.li@uconn.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(given = "Kun", family = "Chen", role = "aut"),
    person(given = "Jun", family = "Yan", role = "aut"))
Description:
    Implements the method proposed by Li and Li (2026) for detection and
    attribution analysis of climate change using polynomial shrinkage under
    variance heterogeneity. The framework models a common covariance structure
    for observations, forced simulations and control runs, while allowing their
    internal variability magnitudes to differ. Estimates forcing scaling factors
    and variance inflation factors for forced simulations and control runs
    relative to observations, and selects polynomial shrinkage by minimizing
    the estimated total asymptotic variance of the scaling factor estimator.
    Provides asymptotic confidence intervals and approximate residual consistency
    diagnostics. The equal-variability model is available by fixing both inflation
    factors at one. Retains earlier total least squares and estimating equation
    methods (Li et al., 2025, <doi:10.1175/JCLI-D-24-0193.1>;
    Ma et al., 2023, <doi:10.1175/JCLI-D-22-0681.1>) for comparison and
    reproducibility, together with covariance shrinkage estimators.
